<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Paladin Role Play</h1>
<p>These are ideas for the roleplayer to consider when playing a Paladin character in Valhalla. None of these are set in stone for the individual. For example the conflict of a Groll Paladin might make an interesting role.
</p>
<ul><li>Paladins are honorable in a fight, waiting for a worthy opponent to retrieve a lost weapon or giving them a chance to surrender in a fight.</li>
<li>They tend to mistrust users of magic and dismiss their feats as trickery as the power is not from the divine.</li>
<li>Most Paladins are human as the longer lived races shy away from the fanaticism associated with the Church Knights.</li>
<li>Holy Knights consider grolls, goblins and kobolds as the spawn of evil. As such they do not trust them in general and seek to destroy them.</li>
<li>Most Paladins are fairly poor, giving their worldly goods to those who are in need or the Church. They retain only enough to maintain their weapons, care for their mount and provide for their family and themselves in that order of precedence.</li>
<li>Paladins must perform a Holy Quest or 'give up' a pleasure when they become a full fledged Knight.</li>
<li>If asked for assistance Paladins must comply. The two exceptions to this are if the requestor is evil or the goal is evil, then they must attempt to thwart the request. Usually killing the requester is the most expedient method.</li>
<li>If a Paladin is on a quest or a mission for another, he may give minimal assistance to any request. Assistance is rarely in the form of money, usually in the form of services.</li></ul>
